WEBVTT

00:08:58.996 --> 00:09:01.412
He was of African descent.

00:09:01.454 --> 00:09:03.621
He lived into the middle,
maybe even old age,

00:09:03.662 --> 00:09:06.079
by the time he died in the early 1900s.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:08.371
He was probably born into slavery.

00:09:09.121 --> 00:09:11.454
And so we wonder,
was he brought to Mississippi?

00:09:11.496 --> 00:09:14.954
Was he taken from his family
like so many enslaved children were?

00:09:14.996 --> 00:09:18.537
Or did he come after the Civil War
to make a new life for himself,

00:09:18.579 --> 00:09:19.996
or find family?

00:09:20.037 --> 00:09:22.371
He and the men
with similar life histories,

00:09:22.412 --> 00:09:26.704
migrants who are buried
in grave 18 and grave 219,

00:09:26.746 --> 00:09:28.246
they made a good enough living

00:09:28.287 --> 00:09:30.912
that their families were able
to give them nice burials,